    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T16:36:44Z",
    "body": "Open: Q2.\n\nQ2: Fragment parsing into SVG and MathML `title`, `style`, `script` and `noscript` treats comments and processing instructions as text, while document parsing keeps them as nodes. So `svgStyle.innerHTML = \"<!-- .a{} -->\"` gives an active rule (CSS skips `<!--` and `-->`), where today it gives a comment, and reading `innerHTML` of an SVG `style` with a comment child and setting it back turns the comment into text. Should fragment parsing keep comments and PIs too?\n\n- (a) Keep comments and PIs in these fragments, and drop those containing `</`, since the context element's end tag isn't recognized in the fragment, and serializing such a comment would end the element ([spec](https://github.com/zcorpan/html/compare/a7bfa383f06e4b484030da2c144362fe78e954f8...46ab9ff5c44b8e6b21863cf1620b49b553bb5140), [test](https://github.com/zcorpan/wpt/compare/9fd771bf29b337e1187129c08462c7f98a7511e6...5e61359a4726620fdcd021e51552c8b83348ed2d)). Matches document parsing and today's result for comments without `</`, but drops those with it silently (`a<!-- </style> -->b` gives \"ab\"). A DOCTYPE there is dropped, as in document parsing.\n- (b) Keep as is (text only). Simpler and drops nothing, but differs from document parsing, and from today for comments.\n\n<details><summary>Reviewed commits</summary>\n\nReviewed at a7bfa38 on 3941bb4, with web-platform-tests/wpt#65512 at 9fd771b, using spec-pr-review.\n</details>",
